# Root-level ignores for the monorepo. backend/ and frontend/ each have
# their own .gitignore (scaffolded by Laravel/Vite) that's more specific
# to their tooling — this file only covers things at the repo root and a
# safety net for secrets that should never land in any subfolder.

# Composer bootstrap binary — not project source, downloaded fresh by
# DEPLOYMENT.md's setup steps rather than committed.
/composer.phar

# Safety net: never commit an actual .env from anywhere in the tree, only
# .env.example files. backend/.gitignore already covers backend/.env
# specifically; this catches any stray copy elsewhere.
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local scratch/test artifacts that sometimes get created alongside a
# quick manual test (e.g. a throwaway CSV) — never intentional to commit.
*.local.csv
